div.p:
The Third LeſſonLesson that you are to learn by the Rod, (or by the raging PeſtilencePestilence,) is to view the Rod on every ſideside;

 if there be bryers on one ſideside of the Rod, there is RoſemaryRosemary on the other ſideside of the Rod; if there be wormwood and gall at one end of the Rod, there is ſweetsweet honey at the other end of the Rod, as there was at the top of Jonathan's 
               1 Sam. 14. 43. Rod.

I commend that ſpeechspeech of Bernard, NanquamNunquam abs te, abſ
que abſqueabsque te recedo: I never come to theeThee, but by theeThee;
Bern. epiſtepist. 116. I never come from theeThee, without theeThee.

Let a man ſinsin in the cloſeſtclosest retirement that humanehuman policy can contrive;
let him take all the wayesways he can to hide his ſinssins, to cloak and cover his ſinsin,sin as Adam did;, yet ConſcienceconscienceConscience will ſoso play the Judge,judge that it will bring in the evidence, produce the Lawlaw, urge the penalty, and paſspass the ſentencesentence of Condemnationcondemnation upon him. There is many a man who makes a fair profeſſionprofession, and who hath a great name in the world, who yet is αὐτοκατάκριτος, 〈 in non-Latin alphabet 〉 αὐτοκατάκριτος,〈 in non-Latin alphabet 〉 ſelfself-condemned for thoſethose ſecretsecret ſinssins which are not obvious to the eyes of man, nor puniſhablepunishable by the Lawslaws or hands of men;. yeaYea, many times in this lifelife, God raiſethraiseth ſuchsuch a hell of horror &and terror in many mens ConſciencesConsciences,men’s consciences by reaſonreason of their ſecretsecret ſinssins, that they can have no reſtrest nor quiet, neither at bed nor at board, neither lying down nor riſingrising up; fain. Fain would they would conceal their ſinssins, unwilling they are that the world ſhouldshould know how vile they have been in ſecretsecret;. butBut ConſcienceconscienceConscience being upon the rack, and ſtillstill aa- gnawing, accuſingaccusing, &and condemning of them, they can hold no longer;.
nowNow all muſtmust out;, and now thoſethose ſinssins that were moſtmost ſecretsecret &and concealed come to be publiſhedpublished upon the houſehouse-tophousetop.
